# Implementation choices

Prefer one way to do each job. Do not add a second library or API for a purpose this project already covers.

This is not an absolute ban. A second method may stay, or be added, when there is a clear reason (a real constraint the current choice cannot meet). An existing outlier is not a license to copy it into new code.

## When the choice is unclear

Stop. Show the tradeoff between the options, ask for approval, and wait. Do not add the second method before that answer. Then follow the instruction.

## Current choices

| Purpose | Use | Do not add |
|---|---|---|
| Unique random strings | `nanoid` | `crypto.randomUUID`, another id library |
| YAML read and write | `yaml` (eemeli/yaml) | `js-yaml` |

New code and newly chosen dependencies follow this list. Do not rewrite existing call sites only to align them.
